# Open Roark Ironbeard's shop and walk the selection down the list, then back
# up to the top. This is the oracle for inc-upw.23.
#
#   tools/headless.sh tools/keys/store-scroll.keys 1
#
# The shop is reached without wizard mode: the cave entrance in
# lib/dungeon.irh:203 asks "Store, Inn, Retire or Descend?" on EV_ENTER, and
# [s] calls InitShopkeeper($"Roark Ironbeard",100000) and throws EV_BARTER.
# Roark's Gear list (lib/dungeon.irh:308) is long enough to overflow the
# window, which is what the bug needs.
#
# Five screen dumps. The comparison between them is the whole test:
#
#   store-open    the list as it first appears, selection on row 00.
#   examine-top   [x] on row 00, so the check knows what row 00 looks like.
#   store-down    after 40 DOWN presses. The selection is far below row 00,
#                 so the page MUST have scrolled and row 00 MUST be gone.
#   examine-down  [x] again. It MUST differ from examine-top, or the DOWN
#                 keys never reached the menu and the run measured nothing.
#   store-up      after 40 UP presses. The selection is back on row 00, so
#                 the page MUST have scrolled back and row 00 MUST be there.
#
# Before the fix, all three are the same page: PartialRedraw calls
# ClearScroll(true), which zeroes TextTerm::offset, and every arrow key jumps
# back to PartialRedraw. See tools/check_store_scroll.sh.

@include chargen.keys

@until "Store, Inn, Retire or Descend" <
s                   # [s] Store

@dump:store-open
x                   # [x] examine the selected row -- row 00
@dump:examine-top
ESC                 # close the description box

DOWN*40
@dump:store-down
x                   # examine again: a DIFFERENT description proves curr moved
@dump:examine-down
ESC

UP*40
@dump:store-up

ESC                 # leave the shop
@quit
